    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear what u say about the hybrid model but some people in the office are pushing back. they think focusing strictly on the lowest income levels actually hurts the 'missing middle'—like teachers or service workers who make too much for the priority stuff but still can't afford the city. isn't it actually more equitable to use transit proximity or just a flat lottery so you aren't constantly moving the goalposts on what 'need' looks like? why is the income-based way better than those?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
