      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While a flat lottery or transit priority offers fairness in distribution, an income-based model directly aligns with the legal mandate to serve \"affordable\" housing, which is specifically defined by low to moderate income limits. If the policy is too broad, it may include households that can easily work their way into the private market, effectively \"moving the goalposts\" on who the program is truly designed to support. The most defensible and equitable strategy often involves a clear income cap that recognizes the \"missing middle\" but still prioritizes those whose financial need is most acute to prevent resource dilution.",
